  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Search, Detection, Navigation, Guidance, Aeronautical, and Nautical System and Instrument Manufacturing (NAICS 334511) has recorded $11.2B in federal contract obligations for FY2026 to date. The Department of Defense is the dominant buyer, obligating $9.1B, followed by the Department of Transportation with $1B and the Department of Homeland Security with $840M. The market is concentrated in a relatively small set of prime contractors, led by RAYTHEON COMPANY at $1.6B and LOCKHEED MARTIN CORPORATION at $866M. Obligations fell 39.1% year over year. Annual obligations rose across FY21 to FY25, moving from $13.2B in FY21 to $18.4B in FY25, then declined to $11.2B in FY26 to date. The FY2026 award landscape includes 6,820 awards with an average award size of $1.6M. Buyers range from large defense customers to civilian agencies such as the Department of Energy, which obligated $40.2M, and the National Aeronautics and Space Administration, which obligated $27.8M, reflecting cross-government demand for navigation and sensing systems.",
    "sections": [
      {
